  "question": "Can the complete public eight-volume 1959 Beijing Library rare-book catalog scans be machine-searched for printed 3288 strongly enough to support a whole-catalog negative or explain the target-specific 3368 -> 3288 change?",
  "answer": "No. The complete eight-volume public scan set is mapped, but the tested machine-navigation layers fail positive calibration. The successful r5 eight-volume run emitted zero 3288 candidates in every volume, yet on volume 1 it also failed to recognize the already directly and manually closed positive controls on PDF55-56, including 3368. A separate pdftotext calibration shows the known-positive pages have no embedded text layer or fonts, and both a 48-variant conventional OCR calibration and a 64-variant native Traditional-Chinese vertical OCR calibration produce zero positive variants on the same known-positive pages. Therefore every zero-candidate result is non-evidentiary for absence. Batch 12HZ/12IA remain controlling: the observed 3368 -> 3288 change is target-specific inside a stable local neighborhood, but its causal mechanism is unresolved.",
